{{head|yol|verb form}}

# [[am]]
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|chapter=CASTEALE CUDDE'S LAMENTATION|number=4|page=104|title=SONGS, ETC. IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage=Fan ich '''aam''' in this miseree.|translation=When I '''am''' in this misery.}}
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|chapter=ABOUT AN OLD SOW GOING TO BE KILLED|number=1|page=106|title=SONGS, ETC. IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage="Murreen leam, kish am." Ich '''aam''' goan maake mee will.|translation=To my grief, I am a big old sow. I '''am''' going to make my will,}}
